            <ArticleTitle>Drug management of chronic benign pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic benign pain usually requires treatment with drugs. Three main classes of drugs are used: opiates, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, and a miscellaneous group which includes psychoactive drugs and a variety of specific agents for individual conditions. The careful selection and combination of drugs, with adequate and appropriate dosage, will bring pain relief in the majority of patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
